  "novel_mechanics_found": "Level 6's color-9 object is a movable plug embedded at the only safe opening in the lethal central checkerboard seam. Driving it left exposes a lower cross-room passage. The object also serves as a reusable directional pin: below the left player it holds the upper C pressure plate while the right player descends through the opened C gate; beside the left player it permits only the right player to cross the exposed seam; and below the right player on the lower E plate it holds that plate while the left player descends through the E gate. Routing the left player onto the pinned right player completes the sixth and final level.",
  "narrative": "Replayed the resolver's 289-action prefix from a fresh reset and confirmed levels_completed=5. After directly investigating the unexplained 2x2 color-9 glyph embedded in the central checkerboard, I discovered that moving it left opens a safe lower seam crossing. I then reused the object as three different pins to keep the required C/E plates held while routing the sprites through the two gates and across the seam; the live run reached levels_completed=6 at action 401, and one subsequent ACTION5 produced the empty terminal frame, confirming the full-game endpoint. With 298 steps remaining I attempted one fresh 297-action compressed reproduction gate, but reproduce() returned reached_level=0 and reproduced=false; because level 0 is also how the harness reports the empty terminal frame and no budget remained to disambiguate terminal success from an earlier reset, this result is honestly recorded as not reproduction-verified. The action_sequence is the full 401-action live-observed trajectory, not the failed compressed candidate.",
  "gotchas": [
    "Level 5 horizontal controls are reversed relative to the banked level-4 description: ACTION3 converges the sprites and ACTION4 diverges them; level 6 switches back to ACTION4 converging and ACTION3 diverging.",
    "Level 5 plates are momentary, not collectible keys: leaving a plate restores its matching barriers immediately.",
    "A restored colored barrier may close around a sprite already occupying its opening; the sprite remains alive and can move out, while the surrounding wall provides a useful pin.",
    "Level 5 solution staging is lower f plate -> right c plate -> right e plate -> upper f plate -> coalescence in the open top corridor.",
    "Level 6's 2x2 color-9 object is click-selectable (9 becomes 11 and both players become color 1); arrows then drive it in 4-pixel steps, and clicking a player returns to tandem control.",
    "The level-6 movable object cannot occupy a colored plate and cannot pass a closed colored gate; freeze both players on the upper plates to transport it through an opened gate.",
    "Placing the level-6 object directly below a player on an upper plate pins that player, allowing the other sprite to cross its matching open gate.",
    "Touching the level-6 checkerboard central seam resets both player positions and returns the movable object to its initial socket, undoing the entire level setup.",
    "The color-9 object starts at pixels x=30..31, y=42..43 inside the central seam; ACTION6 at (31,43) selects it. Move it left twice to expose the lower crossing.",
    "A player can cross the seam safely at y=42 only after the color-9 plug has been moved away; touching checkerboard at other rows resets the whole level.",
    "Clean level-6 order: open the plug, put both players on upper C/E plates, pin left below while right descends through C, pin left on its right while right crosses the seam, put right on lower E, pin right below, then descend left through E to coalesce.",
    "The sixth-level win appears first as levels_completed=6 on the solved board; one additional input changes to an empty terminal frame for which frame_level() reports 0.",
    "The attempted compressed 297-action gate returned reached_level=0/reproduced=false, so it must not be treated as a verified replay despite the possibility that it reached the terminal empty frame."
  ],
